            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "QUILTQUEEN"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Based on others' suggestions, I modified things a little and it turned out fantastic! I reduced the lemon juice and Worcestershire to 1/2 tsp. each, only used one clove of garlic (we're not big fans), added 2 Tblsp. of mayo, used seasoned salt instead of plain, added a little cayenne and a little Old Bay. Let it sit overnight and served it cold with crackers. It disappeared quickly, no leftovers. Yum!",
            "datePublished": "2016-11-25T20:36:55.880Z"
          },
